Benjamin Schieder <blindcoder@scavenger.homeip.net> writes:
> Darshan Shaligram wrote:
[Vecna is MR_PLUSFOUR, only +4 weapons can damage him]
>> The question is, does anybody like this MR_PLUSX business?

> Haven't met them in any RPG so far and yes, I quite like it.

Hmm, isn't this a C?RPG concept? I can't say offhand where I've heard
of this before. Doesn't A?D&D have this sort of rule? (I've never
played D&D of any kind, so don't shoot me if I'm wrong. :-)) I
distinctly remember a friend who's a major fan of Neverwinter Nights
cursing this feature. Maybe NWN has this, or something similar?

> Vecna is a wimp iff you can hurt him. And it's quite the challenge
> for my illiterate weaponless vegetarian (yummy royal jelly) neutral
> monk :)

It's just that this MR_PLUSX introduces an utterly unnatural damage
curve, and confuses a great many new players.

Vecna's wimpiness should probably be remedied by rebalancing the
game. Right now the behaviour looks black and white: either you can
hurt Vecna, in which case he's a pushover, or you can't scratch him at
all. This doesn't strike me as a happy balance.

I'd rather see the MR_PLUSfoos thrown out of the game altogether, and
while we're about it, get rid of Elbereth as well (decoupling Elbereth
from crowning may make this more palatable). I believe that
combination would serve game balance better. Thoughts?

